  "description": "For this brunch cocktail—Canada’s answer to the Bloody Mary—we skip the Clamato and use a blend of tomato juice, bottled clam juice, Worcestershire sauce, plus umami-rich fish sauce and optional MSG to bolster the drink’s savory appeal.",
  "notes": "Total time, including resting: 2 hr 10 min.\n\nOptional or for serving: Pinch of monosodium glutamate (MSG), optional; Dash of Tabasco, optional; Freshly cracked black pepper, optional\n\nOptional substitutions: Lemon wedges → lime wedges; Cubed chunks of Parmesan cheese → shattered chunks of Parmesan cheese\n\nNotes: 3 3/4 cups Clamato can be substituted for the tomato and clam juice. If using Clamato, omit the optional monosodium glutamate (MSG).\n\nMake-ahead and storage: The Bloody Caesar mix can be made through step 1 and refrigerated for up to 2 days.",
